    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Up front next, the breaking news as the nation warns the 21 lives lost in Texas, growing questions over the police response to the shooter, and the messages he sent just before the massacre. Plus, a Republican who represented the people of Yvaldi, now he's calling out his own party for doing nothing about gun violence, saying quote, the shit has got to stop. Will Hurt is my guest tonight. Plus more calls for arming teachers and security guards at schools. Is there any evidence though that that works? We investigate. Let's go out front. And good evening, I'm Erin Bernad, out front tonight, at least 40 minutes of terror. Officials now say the gunman who murdered 19 children and two teachers was inside the Uvoli Texas Elementary School for more than 40 minutes, if not longer. During that time, he murdered 21 innocent people, the families of the children you see on your screen, torn apart in a matter of seconds. Their parents, brothers and sisters, friends, we'll never see them again. And yesterday's attack has now brought the number of shootings of four or more people in the United States to 213 incidents this year alone. 213 incidents where four or more people have been shot. I mean, to put that into perspective, today is the 145th day of the year, which, just to do the very basic comparison, means there have been more mass shootings than days. in the year 2022. And there have been at least 30 shootings at K through 12 schools already this year. This is unacceptable, but we must say it. It is the reality. And because there has been no action time after time after time again, it actually is accepted. And today we heard from Texas Governor Greg Abbott. He says the government was a high school dropout with no known history of mental health problems. An 18-year-old that we now know, according to investigators, sent a message online 30 minutes before the shooting, saying he was going to shoot his grandmother. Minutes later, the gunman wrote, quote, I shot my grandmother. And 15 minutes before the shooting, he writes, quote, I'm going to shoot an elementary school. All right, so these are the pieces of information we're now piecing together. As we also learn a school, resource officer confronted the gunman at Rob Elementary School, but no gunfire was exchanged as the shooter entered the school. 21 people then were murdered. It is the deadliest school shooting since Sandy Hook in Connecticut 10 years ago. That attack in 2012 was really about the same time that many of those who were slaughtered yesterday in Texas were born. 10-year-old Lexi Rubio, 10 years old. Her parents just celebrated her making the all-honor role before saying goodbye to her at school yesterday. Her father, who was a deputy, actually was one of the first responders to the shooting. And earlier, her parents spoke to our Jason Carroll about their daughter and her dreams. Ed Lavender is out front. He is live in Uvaldi tonight and Lucy Caffin opposite in San Antonio, where students are still recovering. Obviously some are still we're hoping and praying that they will survive. Ed, let me begin with you. What more are you learning right now?",
