    "turn_text": "Well, Commissioner, I appreciate you. I think you are where I believe the majority of the country is. Thank you so very much, sir. And of course, Candice and Ed, thank you. Next, President Biden is demanding action tonight, saying something needs to be done. But of course, what will be done? Plus better of work running for Texas governor confronts the current governor. And there are an estimated 20,000 armed security guards in America's schools, 20,000. The one in Uvalde was armed. So do they work to stop mass shootings, an out front investigation coming up? Effing nuts to do nothing about this. That was Arizona Senator Mark Kelly's reaction to the last mass shooting in Texas. Kelly's wife, former Congressman Gabby Giffords, was shot in the head in 2011 in a mass shooting in a supermarket parking lot. There have been a lot of strong words on Capitol Hill today, but there has been yet no planned action on gun legislation before Congress leaves town tomorrow for the Memorial Day holiday. The White House tonight, President Biden, is demanding more action.",
