    "turn_idx": 114,
    "turn_text": "is that the American public agrees with both of you. They agree, right? So Monmouth University did a poll after the Parkland shooting in which 17 students and teachers were killed. And what I found fascinating about this, and I remembered it ever since, because the NRA comes out and fights for this absolutism. But the people who are the members of the NRA do not actually support the NRA's public position. 69% in that poll of NRA members supported background checks for all gun purchases. That's 69% of NRA members, 83% of the general population. So how is it? Well, that Republican lawmakers, many of them, do not support expanding background checks. They're at odds with the members of the NRA. Well,",
