    "turn_text": "gun owners. You know, they take several days of training before you get licensed to go hunting. Responsible gun owners lock their guns and the ammunition up so nobody can get access to it. Responsible gun owners know that these things in teach, you know, their children how to properly use this. And so why we're not seeing more movement on these issues. Responsible gun owners do not think terrorists and people that have serious mental health issues should have access to firearms. And so the question is not about responsible gun owners because responsible gun owners agree with all these things. And just today I think that the study came out. About 90% of Americans think something needs to be done. But what we have to prevent is we have to prevent everybody going to their same tired corners and arguing for their same tired case that happens every time one of these things happen. There is not one single solution to this problem. We have to do a lot of things and at the end of the day, today, there are 19 moms that are not going to be able to tuck their children away. And when you got to understand about you, this is a small community. They know everybody. This is not just impacting the families. It's not just impacting the spouses of the teachers that were killed. This is impacting everybody. The police officers that went in and saw the carnage where people had to be ID by DNA. This is going to impact people for a long time to come. The people in Sutherland Springs from a couple years ago are still dealing with the trauma. The people in El Paso are still dealing with trauma. This is happening all over. This is an area where we should be able to get together and say, hey, 50% of teenage kids in this country shouldn't be afraid of something, a major shooting event happening at their school. And if this continues, guess what's happened? It's gonna be harder and harder to get teachers to teach because they're gonna be afraid to be in these schools. So there's a lot of things we can be doing and it requires leadership from Democrats. It requires the GOP, GOP. If you are gonna be the party of law enforcement and be the party of You know, that's tough on crime. Then we got to be tough on mass shootings and have the best ideas on how to prevent this from happening.",
