    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51786.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 139,
    "turn_text": "You know, I remember back after the shooting in Sandy Hook that, you know, how lost we all felt and how we felt like we were in this black hole and would never get out. And there were some survivors from Columbine who came to Newtown and frankly threw us a lifeline. Just the fact that they were alive and functioning and speaking and, you know, there for us let us know that we could get through it. We knew it wasn't going to be pretty. We knew it wasn't going to be easy. We knew it was going to be a tough road. But seeing somebody else who had been there made a significant difference for us and also gave us lifelong friendships that frankly have helped us and continue to help us as we see these things continue to happen.",
